552 0 obj
<</Type/Annot/Subtype/Widget/Ff 8392704/BS<</S/S/W 1>>/T(Text Field49)/Rect[66.143 52.844 567.267 446.829]/V(All analysts involved in the prepping, processing, changeover, and reading of the samples \205 Elysse Nioupin, Sonal Uprety, Gerald Anyangwe, and Varsha Subramanian \205 were interviewed and their answers are recorded throughout this document.\n\nThe sample was stored upon arrival according to the Client\220s instructions. Analysts Elysse Nioupin and Sonal Uprety confirmed the integrity of the samples throughout both the preparation and processing stages. No leaks or turbidity were observed at any point, verifying the integrity of the sample.\n\nAll reagents and supplies mentioned in the material section above were stored according to the suppliers\220 recommendations, and their integrity was visually verified before utilization. Moreover, each reagent and supply had valid expiration dates.\n\nDuring the preparation phase, Elysse Nioupin disinfected the samples using acidified bleach and placed them into a pre-disinfected storage bin. On 07Aug26, prior to sample processing, Sonal Uprety performed a second disinfection with acidified bleach, allowing a minimum contact time of 10 minutes before transferring the samples into the cleanroom suites. A final disinfection step was completed immediately before the samples were introduced into the ISO 5 Biological Safety Cabinet \(BSC\), E001313, located within the middle ISO 7 buffer room, \(Suite 115A\). All activities were performed in accordance with MICRO-SOP-12, Rapid Scan RDI\256 Test using FIFU Method.\n\nThe cleanroom used for testing \(E001737\) consists of three interconnected sections: the innermost ISO 7 cleanroom \(115B\), which opens into the middle ISO 7 buffer room \(115A\), and then into the outermost ISO 8 anteroom \(115\). A positive air pressure system is maintained throughout the suite to ensure controlled, unidirectional airflow from 115B through 115A and into 115.\n\nThe cleanroom used for changeover \(L-Suite\) consists of four interconnected rooms: the innermost ISO 7 cleanroom E001979 \(145\), which opens into the adjacent ISO 7 buffer cleanroom E001978 \(144\), followed by ISO 8 anteroom E001977 \(143\) and the outermost ISO 8 room E001976 \(142\). A positive air pressure system is maintained throughout the suite to ensure controlled, unidirectional airflow from 145 through 144 and 143 into 142.\n\nThe ISO 5 BSC E001313, located in the middle ISO 7 buffer room, \(Suite 115A\), and ISO 5 BSC E001937, located in the adjacent ISO 7 buffer cleanroom, \(L-Suite\), were thoroughly cleaned and disinfected prior to their respective procedures in accordance with MICRO-SOP-9, Cleaning and Disinfecting Procedure for Microbiology. Furthermore, the BSCs used throughout testing, E001313 for sample processing and E001937 for the changeover step, were certified and approved by both the Engineering and Quality Assurance teams. Sample processing was conducted within the ISO 5 BSC in the middle ISO 7 buffer room \(Suite 115A, BSC E001313\) by Sonal Uprety and the changeover step was conducted within the ISO 5 BSC in the adjacent ISO 7 buffer cleanroom \(L-Suite, BSC E001937\) by Gerald Anyangwe on 07Aug26.\n\nThe analyst, Varsha Subramanian, confirmed that the equipment was set up as per ENG-SOP-4 \(Scan RDI\256 System \205 Operations \(Standard C3 Quality Check and Microscope Setup\) and Maintenance\), and the negative control and the positive control for the analyst, Varsha Subramanian, yielded expected results.)/F 4/M(D:20250930131256-06'00')/DA( 0 0 0 rg 0.000 0.000 0.000 RG /Helv 0.000 Tf)/MK<<>>/FT/Tx/NM(401dd15e-4d9b-4545-bcf8-cc1eced1efe4)/AP<</N 553 0 R>>>>
endobj

