0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(One CFU was recovered from processing analyst Sonal Uprety's right-hand touch plate and submitted for ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(microbial identification under sample ID ETX-260817-0447. The isolate was identified as Micrococcus luteus. ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(This recovery was not microbiologically consistent with the organism observed in the test sample: Micrococcus ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(luteus is coccal in morphology, whereas the microorganism recovered from the test sample exhibited ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(rod-shaped morphology. Accordingly, the personnel monitoring result does not support direct transfer of the ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(recovered right-glove organism to the test sample. In contrast, personnel monitoring for changeover analyst ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Gerald Anyangwe yielded no microbial growth.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Two CFUs were also recovered from settling plate Settling 1 within BSC E001313 and submitted for microbial ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(identification under sample ID ETX-260817-0507. The isolates were identified as Sporisorium graminicola and ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Ustilago maydis. These microorganisms are fungal species, which are taxonomically and morphologically ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(distinct from the bacterial rod-shaped microorganisms recovered from the test sample. Additionally, the settling ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(plate was documented as desiccated at the 5-day read. Therefore, no microbiological match exists between the ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(settling-plate isolates and the test-sample contaminant. Settling plates within changeover BSC E001937 yielded ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(no growth. This finding was evaluated in conjunction with the remaining contemporaneous environmental ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(monitoring data, including the complete absence of microbial recovery from all ISO 5 work surfaces within both ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(BSC E001313 and BSC E001937.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Routine weekly facility monitoring during the week of testing recovered 1 CFU of Gram-positive short rods from ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(active air monitoring in ISO 8 Cleanroom 115 \(ETX-260817-0370\) and 2 CFUs identified as Bacillus megaterium ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(from the floor of ISO 7 Suite 115A \(ETX-260817-0366\). In the L-Suite, routine weekly surface sampling of ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(cleanroom Room 144 \(CR1978\) yielded no microbial growth, while active air monitoring recovered typical ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(human-associated flora \(Staphylococcus, Micrococcus, Corynebacterium spp.\) strictly confined to ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(lower-classified background areas \(ISO 8 anteroom 143 and outer room 142\). All of these recoveries occurred in ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(lower-classified background areas physically separated from the critical ISO 5 testing zones. Furthermore, the ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(positive pressure cascade \(flowing outwards from ISO 7 rooms 145 and 144 toward ISO 8 rooms 143 and 142\) ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(and the transfer of samples in disinfected, closed containers provide robust barriers preventing ingress of ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(airborne contaminants into the ISO 5 work areas. The complete absence of microbial recovery on all ISO 5 ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(critical surfaces within both BSCs further demonstrates that environmental controls effectively prevented transfer ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(into the critical testing zone.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Monthly cleaning and disinfection, using H2O2, of the cleanrooms \(ISO 7\) and their containing Biosafety ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Cabinets \(BSCs, ISO 5\) were performed on 26Jul26, as per MICRO-SOP-9, Cleaning and Disinfecting ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Procedure for Microbiology. It was documented that all H2O2 indicators passed.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Analyzing a 6-month sample history for GoGoMeds Select \(E10747\), this specific analyte "Tirzepatide/B12 ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(25/1mg/mL Injectable" has had no prior failures using the Scan RDI method during this period.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(To evaluate the potential for sample-to-sample contamination, all samples processed on the same day were ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(reviewed. All other samples processed by the same analyst and by other analysts on that day yielded negative ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(results, indicating that cross-contamination is unlikely.) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(Based on the cumulative evidence, it is highly unlikely that the failing results were due to reagents, supplies, the ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(cleanroom environment, the process, or analyst involvement. Consequently, the possibility of laboratory error ) Tj
0 -11.160001 Td
/Helv 10 Tf
(contributing to this failure is minimal. Therefore, the original test result is deemed valid.) Tj
